From: Kiwibot JP5 bring-up <pedro@kiwibot.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Sep 2026 12:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tegra210_adsp (sound/soc/tegra): do not rename the registered adsp_audio device

Same bug as in nvidia/sound/soc/tegra-alt/tegra210_adsp_alt.c, in the copy the kernel actually
builds (CONFIG_SND_SOC_TEGRA210_ADSP -> sound/soc/tegra/tegra210_adsp.c). dev_set_name() on the
already registered of_platform child "adsp_audio" kfree()s the old kobject name that
platform_device.name still points to; every later platform_match() (any module load) then reads
freed memory (KASAN: use-after-free in strcmp, Freed by tegra210_adsp_audio_probe).
---
 sound/soc/tegra/tegra210_adsp.c | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/sound/soc/tegra/tegra210_adsp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/tegra/tegra210_adsp.c
@@ -4511,10 +4511,9 @@
 
 	pr_info("%s: platform probe started\n", __func__);
 
-	if (dev_set_name(&pdev->dev, "%s", DRV_NAME) < 0) {
-		dev_err(&pdev->dev, "error in setting adsp device name\n");
-		return -ENODEV;
-	}
+	/* Do not dev_set_name() a registered device: it frees the old name that
+	 * platform_device.name still references (use-after-free in platform_match).
+	 * Keep the DT-derived name "adsp_audio". */
 
 	match = of_match_device(tegra210_adsp_audio_of_match, &pdev->dev);
 	if (!match)
